    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_0f2870d6cab770268823ea3153ce5652798a9bb38fff5b6cc30d4edeb69bd24d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The mean estimate is assembled as a transport chain: curvature of the continuously indexed Gram phase yields a uniform cosine-sum cancellation bound; the direct and functional-equation-dual sums are reduced to those oscillations; reordering and partial summation preserve the cancellation under moving truncations and weights; and a σ-dependent transition balances this low-σ analysis against the Dirichlet-series regime to obtain a bound uniform for σ>0.",
