    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1919d5f39a88c994f7a14a2d3db7b39f19ae8ab29405bf4e24cc961ef5a2904d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Restricting the Λ-real foliation to its even-indexed Gram family, Λ and Φ recover the same critical-line phase sections while supplying different off-axis coordinates: the Λ contours are asymptotically horizontal and carry a monotone signed magnitude, whereas the Φ-real contours pass through the same Gram points with asymptotic slope -π/(2 log t).",
